Adapt RDO's rpm-master openstack-keystone.spec to the released 2026.1 tarball
(keystone 29.1.0).

Two unrelated deltas, both caused by upstream moving on while the spec did not:

1. Upstream removed the generated WSGI scripts and the Apache config that went
   with them after 27.x - its own release notes are remove-wsgi-scripts and
   add-keystone-wsgi-module. 29.1.0 ships keystone/wsgi/api.py (an importable
   WSGI application defining "application") and httpd/uwsgi-keystone.conf in
   place of httpd/wsgi-keystone.conf, and pyproject.toml declares only:

       [project.scripts]
       keystone-manage = "keystone.cmd.manage:main"
       keystone-status = "keystone.cmd.status:main"

   This is the single reason RDO's own EL10 keystone build has failed in %prep
   since 27.x, and why the newest keystone installable from centos10-master is
   27.1.0.

2. The spec already strips the self-referential tox dependency ".[ldap,memcache]"
   from tox.ini, because the tox-based buildrequires generator hands tox's deps
   to packaging.requirements, which rejects a bare "." target:

       ValueError: Requirement '.[ldap]' from tox --print-deps-only: py312 is invalid

   keystone 29 renamed that extra to ".[ldap]", so the existing sed no longer
   matches. Widened to match either form. The extras are already covered by the
   spec's own BuildRequires.

NOTE when editing this patch: rpm expands macros inside spec COMMENTS too. A
comment mentioning a macro by name is expanded into %prep and breaks the
generated shell script with "unexpected EOF while looking for matching quote".
That is why the comments above spell macro names out in words.

Note for the deployment shell: with no packaged vhost and no wsgi script, a
Rocky hagistack must write its own httpd config pointing mod_wsgi at
keystone/wsgi/api.py. EL packaging never enabled a vhost anyway.

diff -ur a/keystone/openstack-keystone.spec b/keystone/openstack-keystone.spec
--- a/openstack-keystone.spec	2026-09-28 21:43:13
+++ b/openstack-keystone.spec	2026-09-28 22:12:37
@@ -102,16 +102,22 @@
 find . \( -name .gitignore -o -name .placeholder \) -delete
 find keystone -name \*.py -exec sed -i '/\/usr\/bin\/env python/d' {} \;
 
-# adjust paths to WSGI scripts
-sed -i 's#/local/bin#/bin#' httpd/wsgi-keystone.conf
-sed -i 's#apache2#httpd#' httpd/wsgi-keystone.conf
+# Upstream removed httpd/wsgi-keystone.conf and the generated
+# keystone-wsgi-public and keystone-wsgi-admin scripts after 27.x (release notes
+# remove-wsgi-scripts and add-keystone-wsgi-module). 29.1.0 ships
+# httpd/uwsgi-keystone.conf and the importable keystone.wsgi.api module, so
+# there are no script paths left to adjust.
 
 sed -i /^[[:space:]]*-c{env:.*_CONSTRAINTS_FILE.*/d tox.ini
 sed -i "s/^deps = -c{env:.*_CONSTRAINTS_FILE.*/deps =/" tox.ini
 sed -i /^minversion.*/d tox.ini
 sed -i /^requires.*virtualenv.*/d tox.ini
 
-sed -i '/\.\[ldap,memcache\]/d' tox.ini
+# keystone 29 changed this self-referential tox dep from .[ldap,memcache] to
+# .[ldap]. Either form is rejected by packaging.requirements when the tox-based
+# buildrequires generator parses it, so match both. The extras are already
+# covered by this spec's own BuildRequires.
+sed -i '/^[[:space:]]*\.\[ldap[^]]*\][[:space:]]*$/d' tox.ini
 sed -i 's/fixtures,//g' test-requirements.txt
 sed -i 's/,postgresql//g' test-requirements.txt
 
@@ -157,7 +163,7 @@
 install -p -D -m 755 tools/sample_data.sh %{buildroot}%{_datadir}/keystone/sample_data.sh
 install -p -D -m 755 %{SOURCE5} %{buildroot}%{_bindir}/openstack-keystone-sample-data
 # Install sample HTTPD integration files
-install -p -D -m 644 httpd/wsgi-keystone.conf  %{buildroot}%{_datadir}/keystone/
+install -p -D -m 644 httpd/uwsgi-keystone.conf %{buildroot}%{_datadir}/keystone/
 
 install -d -m 755 %{buildroot}%{_sharedstatedir}/keystone
 install -d -m 755 %{buildroot}%{_localstatedir}/log/keystone
@@ -213,15 +219,13 @@
 %if 0%{?with_doc}
 %{_mandir}/man1/keystone*.1.gz
 %endif
-%{_bindir}/keystone-wsgi-admin
-%{_bindir}/keystone-wsgi-public
 %{_bindir}/keystone-manage
 %{_bindir}/keystone-status
 %{_bindir}/openstack-keystone-sample-data
 %dir %{_datadir}/keystone
 %attr(0644, root, keystone) %{_datadir}/keystone/keystone-dist.conf
 %attr(0755, root, root) %{_datadir}/keystone/sample_data.sh
-%attr(0644, root, keystone) %{_datadir}/keystone/wsgi-keystone.conf
+%attr(0644, root, keystone) %{_datadir}/keystone/uwsgi-keystone.conf
 %dir %attr(0750, root, keystone) %{_sysconfdir}/keystone
 %dir %attr(0750, root, keystone) %{_sysconfdir}/keystone/policy.d
 %config(noreplace) %attr(0640, root, keystone) %{_sysconfdir}/keystone/keystone.conf
